<title>USA: Delaware majority leader introduces flat tax bill.</title>
<headline>Delaware majority leader introduces flat tax bill.</headline>
<dateline>DOVER, Del. 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delaware House Majority Leader Wayne Smith late Thursday proposed a flat tax for the state.</p>
<p>Smith said the plan would eliminate Delaware's current tax code and replace it with a flat, 4.5 percent tax rate. In addition, the first $3,000 of income would be tax-exempt.</p>
<p>The Legislature is expected to consider the measure in the next few weeks.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
